WEBVTT

00:00:01.537 --> 00:00:04.287
There's a game-losing blunder
in almost every amateur game.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.110
But what is the most effective way
to improve tactics?

00:00:07.383 --> 00:00:09.973
First of all, if you're under 2000 rating,

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:13.143
improving tactics is the most important thing,
by far.

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:16.783
Position and strategy don't matter
when somebody blunders even once.

00:00:17.253 --> 00:00:20.553
But there are two types of tactics,
and I'll tell you which one you should train.

00:00:21.043 --> 00:00:23.823
There are calculations, which is
your ability to calculate

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.643
and visualize a complicated move.

00:00:26.063 --> 00:00:27.353
This is your active thinking.

00:00:27.843 --> 00:00:30.653
But let's be real.
If you look at your last ten losses,

00:00:30.853 --> 00:00:32.873
you didn't lose due to
a complicated attack.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.543
You lost because of a simple blunder

00:00:35.543 --> 00:00:37.463
or because you missed
a simple tactic to win a piece.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:41.163
What you need is a training method
that improves your pattern recognition.

00:00:41.653 --> 00:00:46.123
That's your brain's ability to instantly
recognize a pattern without having to calculate first.

00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:49.313
Look, you don't have to calculate
to see this checkmate.

00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:51.523
That's pattern recognition.

00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:54.363
Some people try to improve
with tactical puzzles.

00:00:54.843 --> 00:00:58.283
But they're mostly improving their
calculations with difficult tactics.

00:00:58.723 --> 00:01:00.653
They often end up
with a high puzzle rating.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:02.933
But their real chess rating
doesn't improve.

00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:06.953
Because in a real game, you don't
carefully calculate every move like a puzzle.

00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:09.493
You lack simple pattern recognition

00:01:09.493 --> 00:01:12.013
to spot every single blunder
and simple tactic on both sides.

00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:16.093
Even your higher calculations rely
on recognizing the basic pattern.

00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:18.953
So, you have been training
your calculations,

00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:21.223
but you need to train
your pattern recognition.

00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:24.133
Playing many, many chess games
is one way to do that.

00:01:24.593 --> 00:01:27.623
But you probably don't want to play
for an hour every day for years.

00:01:27.993 --> 00:01:30.753
I made it my mission to find
the most efficient way to improve

00:01:30.753 --> 00:01:33.013
pattern recognition with only
20 minutes per day,

00:01:33.013 --> 00:01:34.163
and I might have found it.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.310
Especially if you blunder a piece
or miss a tactic even once

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.500
in five games, this is made for you.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.360
If you play puzzles and feel like
your high puzzle rating

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.060
isn't converting into a good chess rating,

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.650
this is perfect for you.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.600
If you have a feeling that you could avoid
most mistakes if you paid attention,

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.210
but you get lazy while playing
and blunder by random,

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.420
then pattern recognition training
will be a game changer for you.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:59.330
If your dream playstyle
is to have fun destroying people

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.970
without big opening theory,

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.740
playing crazy lines because
you dominate in tactics,

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.930
this is made for you.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.560
Worst case scenario,

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.200
if you don't like it,
you can cancel any time.

00:02:24.463 --> 00:02:26.923
Now is the time to give it a try
and see if you like it.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.220
And I'll see you inside.
